    directories: ["institutions", "history", "world"], category: "institutions",
    title: "The Great Houses and Legacy Lineages", subtitle: "Surviving records of the families that shaped the Realm",
    classification: "Legacy Archive — Incomplete by Design",
    image: image("oracle/historical/10-silveredge-airship-launch.png", "A Silveredge airship launch preserved in the historical archive."),
    summary: "The Realm's great houses were families, sanctuaries, martial traditions, political networks, and chosen kin. This consolidated record preserves their established identities without declaring their modern leadership, extinction, motives, or future.",
    body: ["Institutional knowledge fragmented after the old command circles fell silent. The names below remain historically attested, but SRX possesses only intersections with their stories—not ownership of their family canon.", "Membership was not always biological. Adoption, marriage, sworn service, mentorship, spiritual kinship, and shared defense created lineages as real as blood. A collapsed government or destroyed estate does not mean a family is extinct."],
    facts: [["Archive Condition", "Fragmentary"], ["Modern Leadership", "Unverified unless explicitly stated"], ["Creator Authority", "Retained by original character creators"], ["Public Rule", "Unknown is not extinct"]],
    sections: [
      { title: "House Silveredge", paragraphs: ["Founded in Silvermoon City by Dark and Light Silveredge, House Silveredge was a protector family built through adoption, service, and shared defense rather than blood alone. It sheltered orphans and survivors of violence, then trained them to protect others.", "Dark Silveredge's death and the internal conflict that followed broke the house's old political structure. Aku, Ayame/Xeria, Zero, Chrono, Graves, and other names survive in connected records. SRX has no basis to declare the wider family extinct or to define what its descendants became during the silence.", "Silveredge records are especially sensitive because names, identities, and affiliations changed across eras. Public entries preserve confirmed intersections; private motives, current loyalties, and family continuations remain with their creators." ]},
      { title: "Swiftwood and Duskwood", paragraphs: ["This elven lineage is rooted around Silvermoon and the eastern territories. Rei L. Swiftwood, also recorded as Duskwood, maintained a tavern and sanctuary that sheltered Sephiroth after the Silveredge fracture and later organized Clans Against RIA.", "Tyreal, Serge, Raien, Cyrus, and Virus Swiftwood appear in surviving files. Present leadership, divisions, and descendants are not verified by SRX." ]},
      { title: "Darkblade, Darkhaven, and Nightwind", paragraphs: ["House Darkblade survives in the archive as an old noble combat lineage represented by Artemis and Chloe Darkblade. Its present membership and territory are unconfirmed.", "House Darkhaven is a vampire noble house associated with the Night Court and Tartanalia's older political order. Ciel, Desta, Dase, Lilith, Raven, and Xeno Darkhaven appear in surviving records. SRX does not assign it a modern council representative.", "House Nightwind is an elven, nature-linked line represented most clearly by Lilith Nightwind, with fragments attributed to Cael Nightwind. Its modern size, territory, and relationship to Darkhaven remain incomplete." ]},
      { title: "The Seisen Line", paragraphs: ["The Seisen are recorded as a small off-world warrior lineage associated with Bejita, Meira, Traga, and other Seisen names. Bejita's duel with Dark Silveredge became a turning point in the Silveredge fracture.", "The old clan structure is recorded as disbanded. SRX does not treat that as proof the lineage or its people ceased to exist." ]},
      { title: "Dragonkin and the Rei Line", paragraphs: ["The Rei line is better understood as a species and kinship structure than a conventional political house. Nexa Rei is the best documented historic head associated with it, with relationships extending through the Weyr and DragonsKeep.", "The Weyr is sovereign. SRX records do not determine its private succession, bonds, or current family life." ]},
      { title: "The Raiku–Makai Family Network", paragraphs: ["The Raiku–Makai line is a mixed political and celestial family network shaped by birth, marriage, adoption, alliance, and succession—not a pure clan. Public records connect Sephiroth Raiku-Makai, Alexander Raiku, Arthas Raiku, Lucia Makai, Jasmine Pyrce, Xanos Ariada, and allied branches.", "Only current public offices are stated as current. Historic family connections do not give SRX authority to narrate private relationships or absent characters." ]}
    ],
    highlights: ["A house may lose territory without losing its people.", "Chosen family is part of Realm family history.", "Silence preserves creator space; it does not invite institutional invention."],
    related: ["silvermoon-city", "dragonskeep", "night-court", "grand-history-of-the-realm"],
    source: "data/srx_database/factions/LEGACY_HOUSES.md"
